==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|peresil}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|petroselīnum}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|πετροσέλῑνον||parsley}}, from {{m|grc|πέτρος||rock, stone}} + {{m|grc|σέλῑνον||celery}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpɑː(ɹ)sli/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-parsley.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
{{rfp|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} A bright green, [[biennial]] [[herb]], ''[[Petroselinum crispum]]'' or ''[[Petroselinum neapolitanum]]'' having either flat or curled leaves.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The leaves of this plant used in Middle Eastern, European, and American cooking.

